From 18df3139b067085130461169b1ab0328b7ceeaf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Redgrave961 <214504937+Redgrave961@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:14:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] SPU: run SPURS jobs and firmware SPU plugins as translated
 code

Nothing in Asura's SPU workload is left to the interpreter (was ~26M
interpreted SPU instructions/s).

- tools/lift_spurs_jobs.py: finds every SPURS job binary in a PPU ELF by
  its four `ila $r2` header words (task images, SPU ELF code linked at LS
  0x3000 and up, are skipped), lifts each relocatable at its link base (the
  ELF segment address, or the base its own brsl/ila self-relocation idiom
  names), bounds raw jobs by control-flow reachability and ELF jobs by
  their sections, and registers them by content. Adapted from the inFAMOUS
  2 port's lift_relocmods.py. CMake: ps3recomp_generate_spu_jobs.
- spu_overlay_register_reloc_content: a relocatable region keyed by its
  code bytes, not by a source EA. Titles copy job binaries to the heap and
  pack several into one transfer, so a GET that starts with the code's
  header, or a dispatch miss whose LS holds the code below it, makes the
  lift resident at that placement; the whole code is compared byte for
  byte before it is used.
- lift_firmware_spu.py --pic: dev_flash SPU plugins MultiStream loads at a
  run-time address (flashMP3.pic, flashATRAC.pic), lifted the same way.
- find_spu_functions: reachable_code_end, and infer_code_end_raw for raw
  images.
- Resident code slots: 4 -> SPU_RESIDENT_CODE_SLOTS (16); a job-chain SPU
  holds its policy module and several job buffers at once.
- SPU_INTERP_STATS reports the first code bytes of each interpreted entry;
  SPU_GET_LS=<lo>:<hi> traces GETs by destination.
- Idle-SPU channel wait logs follow ps3_log_verbose; run.bat defaults
  PS3_VERBOSE=0.
